There is a possibility that JBoss Log Manager could end up silently swallowing exceptions that stop Quarkus from starting up. This has not been observed in Quarkus native image today, but it was observed when experimenting with layered direct native image invocations, but the problem could manifest some other way down the line.

GraalVM can throw {{com.oracle.svm.core.jdk.UnsupportedFeatureError}} instances if it has trouble resolving locales, and this is an Error rather than an Exception. The issue arises when this exception is thrown from within {{ExtHandler.publishToNestedHandlers()}}which has this:

{noformat}} catch (Exception e) {
    reportError(handler, "Nested handler publication threw an exception", e, ErrorManager.WRITE_FAILURE);
} catch (Throwable ignored) {
}{noformat}

As an experiment, patching the Throwable section to do this (like done in {{LoggerNode.publish}}):

{noformat}// Do not silently swallow Errors - report them like LoggerNode.publish() does
final Handler h = handler;
ErrorManager errorManager = AccessController.doPrivileged(
    (PrivilegedAction<ErrorManager>) h::getErrorManager);
if (errorManager != null) {
    Exception e;
    if (t instanceof Exception) {
        e = (Exception) t;
    } else {
        e = new UndeclaredThrowableException(t);
    }
    try {
        errorManager.error("Nested handler publication threw an error", e, ErrorManager.WRITE_FAILURE);
    } catch (Throwable t2) {
        StandardOutputStreams.printError(t2, "Handler.reportError caught an exception");
    }
}{noformat}

Makes the error appear:

